Provenance
----------

This skill is a vendored adaptation of the `improve-codebase-architecture`
skill from Matt Pocock's skills repository.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
  Path:      skills/engineering/improve-codebase-architecture/
  Revision:  9c9f36ccd3995266cd675468af71639c8dde1ec5
  Inspected: 2026-08-17

Upstream's process shape, report shape, editorial voice, frontmatter and Codex
manifest are preserved. Nine things differ:

  1. Vocabulary invocation — replace the upstream Skill-tool wording with this
     repository's `codebase-design` invocation idiom.
  2. Domain grounding repointed — replace hard-coded CONTEXT.md and docs/adr/
     reads with `doc-grounded-questions` and its project-specific doc discovery.
  3. Hotspot rule made concrete — inspect the last 50 non-merge commits and
     widen only when history is scattered or has no meaningful concentration.
  4. Scan becomes a registered dispatch — use one marked Opus/high issue-owner
     scan with a seven-item evidence bar, read-only repository access, at most
     one temporary findings artifact, and an inline fallback.
  5. Candidate contract stated — render zero to five evidence-backed candidates,
     never pad, and treat a truthful no-candidate report as successful.
  6. Report contract extended — add accessible semantic fallbacks and a safe
     repository-data-to-HTML/Mermaid boundary, make report generation failures
     fatal, make browser/CDN failures warnings, and always print the absolute
     report path.
  7. Downstream step replaced — replace upstream `grilling` and `domain-modeling`
     with the `wayfind` fog gate, `worktrees`, `design`, `grill-with-docs`, and a
     stop after recommending the appropriate scope workflow.
  8. Provenance pointer — close SKILL.md with a link to this notice.
  9. Package extensions — add this provenance LICENSE and deployed-behaviour
     evals/evals.json, neither of which exists in the upstream skill directory.

There is no automatic synchronisation with upstream: refreshing this package
means comparing against a newer revision by hand, re-applying the nine
adaptations, and moving the revision recorded above.

The upstream licence follows, reproduced unmodified.

